WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS (read end-to-end before writing native code)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AddWidgetButton.tsx is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL floating action button (FAB):
  - Imports: useTranslation (i18n only), shared {Button, Tooltip} from @/components/ui, Icons.add.
  - Props: onClick: () => void ; isEditing: boolean.
  - The ONLY conditional render branch: `if (isEditing) return null;`  (withdrawn in edit mode — the
    dashboard header's own Add Widget action covers that surface).
  - Otherwise: a circular primary Button (variant="primary" size="lg" reshaped h-14 w-14 rounded-full
    p-0 shadow-xl) holding an h-8 w-8 "+" glyph, wrapped in Tooltip content="Add Widget" side="left",
    aria-label="Add Widget".
  - i18n keys extracted: dashboard.addWidget = "Add Widget"  (single key; used for tooltip + aria-label).
  - NO query hook, NO fetch, NO useEffect — the component binds NO asynchronous data.

PARITY DISPOSITION ON STATES (honesty covenant #2 "no scope narrowing", #9 "no silent drift"):
  The prompt's generic state list (loading/empty/error/stale/offline) is the per-surface template. This
  surface's web source has exactly TWO render branches — visible (default) and hidden (isEditing) — and
  binds no async data. loading/empty/error/stale/offline are therefore NOT APPLICABLE: there is nothing
  to load, go empty, fail, or grow stale. Both real branches are reproduced (no narrowing); the
  inapplicable data-states are NOT synthesized (synthesizing freshness chrome on a static "+" button
  would be drift, not parity). This mirrors the accepted disposition of the sibling P4 surfaces whose
  web source likewise gates the whole surface (e.g. AiUsageCard's off-mode gate → EmptyView).

